From f5e61598bfeceee8ac61cfa5b0b3ef315195968d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessandro Fontana <alessandro.fontana@pm.me>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 17:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/exynos: decon7: only set ALPHA_MUL when a plane alpha is
 in use

WINCONx_ALPHA_MUL multiplies the per-pixel alpha of a window by the plane
alpha programmed in VIDOSD_C. decon_win_set_bldmod(), ported from the
Exynos5433 driver, sets it for every per-pixel blend mode, while
decon_update_plane() writes VIDOSD_C as zero and decon_win_set_bldmod()
only overwrites it when the plane alpha is not opaque.

With an opaque plane alpha, which is what SurfaceFlinger asks for on
every layer, the effective source alpha is therefore alpha * 0 = 0: the
"one minus source alpha" destination coefficient of the blend equation
becomes one, and with A = ONE the window is added to the layers below
instead of being blended over them. On a Galaxy Tab A (2016) running
drm_hwcomposer this shows up as the navigation bar letting the app
underneath through and translucent surfaces pulsing during animations.
Window 0 does not have the bit (only WINCON1..4_ALPHA_MUL_F exist) and
does not show the defect, which matches.

The vendor driver (decon_set_alpha_blending()) only sets ALPHA_MUL when
a plane alpha in (0, 255) and a per-pixel alpha are both in use. Do the
same: keep BLD_PIX and ALPHA_SEL for per-pixel blending and add
ALPHA_MUL only when the plane alpha is not opaque, i.e. exactly when
VIDOSD_C holds a meaningful value.

Signed-off-by: Alessandro Fontana <alessandro.fontana@pm.me>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/exynos/exynos7_drm_decon.c | 13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/exynos/exynos7_drm_decon.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/exynos/exynos7_drm_decon.c
index 0c5f866a61..8c9b6a1b15 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/exynos/exynos7_drm_decon.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/exynos/exynos7_drm_decon.c
@@ -363,7 +363,18 @@ static void decon_win_set_bldmod(struct decon_context *ctx, unsigned int win,
 	case DRM_MODE_BLEND_COVERAGE:
 	case DRM_MODE_BLEND_PREMULTI:
 	default:
-		val |= WINCONx_BLD_PIX | WINCONx_ALPHA_MUL | WINCONx_ALPHA_SEL;
+		val |= WINCONx_BLD_PIX | WINCONx_ALPHA_SEL;
+		/*
+		 * ALPHA_MUL multiplies the per-pixel alpha by the plane alpha
+		 * held in VIDOSD_C. With an opaque plane alpha VIDOSD_C is
+		 * written as zero, so leaving ALPHA_MUL set turns the source
+		 * alpha into zero and the "1 - alpha" destination coefficient
+		 * into one: the window is added to the layers below instead
+		 * of being blended over them. The vendor driver only sets the
+		 * bit when a plane alpha is actually in use.
+		 */
+		if (alpha != DRM_BLEND_ALPHA_OPAQUE)
+			val |= WINCONx_ALPHA_MUL;
 		break;
 	}
 
